; `set` on a name that is no binding at all. A built-in answered the
; silent wildcard (`true` here; `(set + 1)` is the same path, but the
; formatter refuses an operator as a `set` target, and every `.ax` must
; format) and an IMPORTED function was left silent (stage0 had
; anchored its refusal in the other file, which this renderer once could
; not quote), so both checked OK - and `emit-llvm` then refused as
; AX4002 "set target is not a mut binding", whose own help calls it a
; compiler bug. Found 2026-09-27 beside the fuzzer's builtin-name
; findings. Both are AX3012 now, anchored at the target in this file.
(import Str)

(:: builtin Int)
(fn (builtin)
  (let ((mut x 0))
    {
      (set true 1)
      x
    }))

(:: imported Int)
(fn (imported)
  (let ((mut x 0))
    {
      (set strLen 1)
      x
    }))

(:: main Int)
(fn (main)
  (let ((mut x 0))
    {
      (set x 1)
      x
    }))
